  ---                                                                           
  You have 4 tools                                                              

  1. view-conversations.py — see what ALEX has been saying

  Quick look (terminal):
  python3 view-conversations.py list-chats              # who's been chatting?
  python3 view-conversations.py view | less              # scroll through
  everything
  python3 view-conversations.py view 6920669447 | less   # one Telegram user
  python3 view-conversations.py view --search "stock"    # find a keyword
  python3 view-conversations.py view --last 5            # last 5 msgs per convo

  Visual HTML report (opens in browser):
  python3 view-conversations.py view --html                          #
  everything
  python3 view-conversations.py view 6920669447 --html               # one user
  python3 view-conversations.py view --search "market" --html        # keyword
  python3 view-conversations.py view 6920669447 --search "email" --html  #
  combine

  Reports save to reports/2026-02-06/ — one folder per date, never overwritten.

  ---
  2. daily-summary.py — what happened today/any day

  python3 daily-summary.py generate                      # today's summary
  python3 daily-summary.py generate --date 2026-02-04    # specific day
  python3 daily-summary.py generate --force              # overwrite today's
  python3 daily-summary.py backfill                      # regenerate all days

  Summaries save to ~/ALEX_NAVADA/daily/Feb-2026/Friday-06-Feb-2026.md etc.

  ---
  3. backup.sh — backup everything

  bash backup.sh               # full backup: Pi + send to iPhone
  bash backup.sh --local        # Pi only
  bash backup.sh --iphone       # send latest backup to iPhone

  Runs automatically: daily at 4am (Pi), Sunday 3am (Pi + iPhone). Keeps last 8
  backups. Accept on iPhone via Tailscale app > Files.

  ---
  4. sessions/SESSION-LOG.md — what we built on ALEX

  cat sessions/SESSION-LOG.md | less

  Auto-updates every time we commit code to ALEX. Shows every day's work since
  Jan 31.

