Step by step

  1. With your script open in Geany, click Build in the top menu bar
  2. Click Set Build Commands
  3. You'll see a table. Look for the Execute section at the bottom
  4. In the Execute row, set the command to:

  python3 "%f" view --html

  5. Click OK
  6. Now press F5 (or Build > Execute)

  The HTML report will generate and open in your browser.

  ---
  To switch between different reports

  Each time you want to run a different command, go back to Build > Set Build Commands and change
  the Execute line:
  ┌────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  Report you want   │           Set Execute command to           │
  ├────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Full HTML report   │ python3 "%f" view --html                   │
  ├────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Single user report │ python3 "%f" view 6920669447 --html        │
  ├────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Search report      │ python3 "%f" view --search "market" --html │
  ├────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ List chats         │ python3 "%f" list-chats                    │
  ├────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Daily summary      │ python3 "%f" generate                      │
  └────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────┘
  ---
  Faster alternative

  Instead of changing the execute command each time, use Geany's built-in terminal:

  1. Go to View menu
  2. Click Terminal (or tick the checkbox if it's there)
  3. A terminal appears at the bottom of the Geany window
  4. Type commands directly:

  cd ~/ALEX_NAVADA/Manager
  python3 view-conversations.py view --html

  That way you edit at the top, run at the bottom — no config changes needed.

